{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7xtnBkorvDaY8BNvEnH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I withdrew the record on span `u4` as an `atom` gap rather than revising it, so this law is now blocked until the operator decides the gap.\n\n**Why the rule can't be written:** subsection 3 of NRS 484A.480 (span `u5`) requires the lights to include \"at least one flashing red warning lamp visible from the front\". The ontology says a warning lamp has a `facing` (front, rear or side). But rules can only test a warning lamp's colour and whether it is flashing, not which way it faces.\n\n**Why I didn't drop the facing:** without it, a vehicle showing only side or rear red flashing lamps would trigger the duty to yield. That widens a condition, which the rules forbid.\n\n**Why no other atom fits:** `rel.visible` and `rel.bearing` are about where one road user is relative to another, not which way a lamp points. `rel.visible`'s contract also says outright that it does not stand in for a lamp being lit.\n\n**What the gap asks for:** a form of `sig.warning_lamp` in Core that can be read with facing as well, e.g. `sig_warning_lamp [x, colour, mode, facing]`.\n\nThe coder also flagged a second problem that this withdrawal doesn't fix. This run's reading puts no road-user class inside the authorized-emergency-vehicle group, so an ambulance's membership is always unknown. The coder therefore rebuilt `forbid`, `permit` and `blind` on the regulatory-agency vehicle instead. Whoever re-plans this law after the gap is decided will need to deal with that too.\n\nThe withdrawal is in `record.jsonl` in the repair directory."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2163,"cache_read_input_tokens":79290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2163},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"us","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"745a410b-8722-44a2-85a0-233a7b545a34","uuid":"0db7fd00-b9e4-4908-b4bc-f9a9367694f1","timestamp":"2026-11-17T05:40:58.453Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7xtmc3L6KzakknLoX3Z"}
